  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Voice sections retain their assigned parts, but singers may move within their section; chair arrangements must preserve accessible paths and sightlines.\", \"decision\": \"How should chairs be arranged within voice sections?\", \"goal\": \"Make rehearsals easy to attend and prepare for while helping singers use shared rehearsal time effectively.\", \"problem\": \"A community choir is preparing a small program through a series of rehearsals. It has a conductor, willing section leaders, a booking organizer, numbered scores that members may use, and shared practice recordings. The rehearsal room has movable chairs and enough space for short sectional work. Members have varied experience and availability. Musical direction remains with the conductor, and each routine below can operate within any agreed rehearsal schedule.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe conductor listens to a short phrase and then asks singers to adjust chairs within their sections. The final arrangement responds to the room’s sound while preserving each singer’s part and view of the conductor.\nSingers arrange their section’s chairs together using the marked boundaries and sightline guidance before the warmup. The people using the seats can resolve local spacing needs while maintaining the common room layout.\nSection leaders arrange chairs before rehearsal and invite singers to choose places within their voice sections. The basic layout is ready on arrival while members retain some control over nearby listening partners and comfort."
    }
  ],
